Finally, I'm back in rgrn. And I have a little story to tell. :-)

The story goes back to 2002 when I started to play priests almost
exclusively. I managed to raise two promising chars, one choked in the
Castle, the other one died on the right High Altar when I tried to
tame Pestilence.

I started playing on nethack.alt.org, which is quite funny, especially
when you go downstairs and are surrounded by a horde of master mind
flayers.

The first few levels were more or less uneventful, the first
interesting thing was an armor shop that provided me with speed
boots. On DL 12 or so I encountered a bones file that was infested
with black puddings. Luckily, I had a wand of fire with me, so the
puddings could not do me any harm. After killing all the puddings with
a club I was very happy to see that the deceased pudding farmer had
left some nice equipment. I found a magic marker, some useful armor
and lots of spellbooks. Of course, there was an altar nearby, which
provided be with Mojo as the first present. Armed with that and poison
resistance I entered the Mines and found a magic lamp there which gave
me a GSDM.

The Quest was quite easy, although food started to be a little
problem. Nevertheless, I managed to gain a few levels there. When I
had the Mitre of Holiness, I accidentally on the lava and lost my
fully enchanted speed boots, but I had a +0 pair still in my
backpack. Since I did not have intrinsic fire resistance I would have
been instantly killed if I didn't have the MoH! Phew.

Medusa and the Castle were rather unspectacular, and I proceeded
quickly into Gehennom. It was my first 3.4.x game in which I
encountered a named demon, so I was a little bit surprised to see them
teleporting away even when I occupied the upstairs. Orcus could only
use one charge of his wand, leaving me with 6 shots before recharging.

I woke Rodney just before turn 40,000 and decided to lure him away
from the water so that the Book of the Dead would not fall into
it. That cost me some time and left him able to gate in lots of
monsters, but my ring of conflict proved to be handy there. Finally, I
finished him off, and ran downstairs since I could not do a controlled
levelport. He showed up twice on the way down (and he is much tougher
without the upstairs trick) and again when I entered the
Sanctum. After a few hits he teleported to the High Priest and left me
alone. I slowly fought my way towards the amulet and discovered the
Mojo really sucks there (when I ascended my Valk, I didn't notice this
that much).

The High Priest gave me some serious hits, reducing my HP from 400 to
130. When he was finally dead, I killed the double-trouble Rodneys
with a single shot from my /WoD. On my way up the mysterious force
didn't annoy me much, even though I was neutral.

Earth was easy and Rodney showed up there for the last time. Air
brought me into serious trouble as you can no longer teleport while
being swallowed. I started using my /WoD against the air elementals,
and jumped into the portal when I ran out of charges. On Fire I
recharged it and headed straight for the portal as it was near my
starting position. Water was harmless again since I had genocided ;s.

On Astral I first headed for the left altar which was guarded by
Death. Why didn't somebody tell me that he is now able to drain
maximum hitpoints? The altar turned out to be wrong and I lost about
100 max HPs in two encounters. The second altar was guarded by
Pestilence (I /WoDed him) and wasn't the correct one, too. I then
rushed to the last altar, tamed a dragon standing next to me and
offered the Amulet.

Finally, after more than a year trying (although I didn't play at all
most of the time), I can now say:

